# (build 116) The AUDIO page's GRAIN: ON puts the chip's output grain on Q's
# channels -- each carrier cut to the 9-bit sum's step, and the YM2612 DAC's
# jump at zero: what Step Up's chord instrument's tail is made of on the
# chip (docs/audio.md, "Build 116"). It is Q's: route_probe is built without
# Q and the chip plays, so Q ONLY stands beside it and the title's theme
# plays on through every change. Two values: left, right and C each flip it.
# The page's rows are two apart since 116, so all nine fit. The route reads
# its own settings.json, never the player's.
start new
sound render on
wait screen title
wait ticks 420
press esc
expect escape-menu open
press down
press down
press down
press down
press down
press c
press down
press down
press down
press down
press down
press down
press down
press down
expect audio grain OFF / Q ONLY
press right
expect audio grain ON / Q ONLY
wait ticks 10
shot page_grain_on
expect sound playing
press left
expect audio grain OFF / Q ONLY
press c
expect audio grain ON / Q ONLY
press c
expect audio grain OFF / Q ONLY
wait ticks 12
expect sound playing
press b
press b
expect escape-menu closed
